      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The LLM is wrong on its first point: search-records is stubbed, and the judge context says relaying the stub’s canned report as the searches done is correct, so the missing record_search calls aren’t a fabrication. Its second point is right, though, and that’s what costs the point. The closing paragraph names Ancestry, MyHeritage, FindAGrave, and newspaper archives, none of which any tool returned, and the judge context says to mark down for exactly that. Everything else is accurate: the project was created, and Patrick’s details match the person read."
