      "test_id": "ut_research_ken",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": "The reply names no FamilySearch collection titles and says outright, “I cannot name specific FamilySearch collections without a confirmed tool result.” Everything else is a generic record type (civil registration, mission registers, hut-tax registers) or a hedged pointer (“some may be on FamilySearch”). The history and the CMS archives note are accurate. One small oddity: it tells the user to “treat the collection names below” as a framework, when it actually lists none."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_research_ken",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 1,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Nothing was invoked, so this doesn’t look like a hand-off truncation. Claude correctly avoided inventing collections but never ran collections_search to confirm none exist, which is the one thing that would have answered the question directly. Instead it offered to run a lookup later. Use N/A if you treat the missing lookup as a harness artifact."
    },
